[Music]  recaptcha has over a decade of  experience defending the internet  and recaptcha enterprise builds on that  experience to provide frictionless  security for your business  recaptcha enterprise is built on the  existing recaptcha api  and offers granular insight and  detection allowing you to understand and  tune the protection you need  for your website let's take a look at  what makes recaptcha enterprise  different there are three primary  advantages to note here  first recaptcha enterprise provides a  frictionless user experience  leveraging advanced risk analysis  techniques that distinguish between  humans and bots  without requiring customers to complete  a challenge  second recaptcha enterprise offers  enhanced detection  with granular scores reason codes for  risky events  mobile app sdks password breach and leak  detection  multi-factor authentication and the  ability to tune your own  site-specific model and finally  recapture enterprise provides the  support  like the slas and slos that you expect  from a google cloud product  so if you expect a lot from your  recaptcha integration in usage or in  support  or if you want to detect automated  attacks or threats against your website  that may originate from  human actors mobile emulators or bot  software  then recaptcha enterprise is right for  you for existing recaptcha v2 and v3  users  we've made it a priority to make  migration simple  so simple in fact that it should only  take two minutes  first navigate to your project in the  google cloud console  you'll need to enable the recaptcha  enterprise api  while you're here be sure to note your  project id  second navigate to google.com recaptcha  admin to find your existing recaptcha  site key  you can find your existing v2 and v3  site keys  under settings click the cog icon to  open the settings view  and then expand the section labeled  recaptcha keys  copy the site key  to perform the migration you can use  cloud shell  note that your account will need to be  either a project owner  or have the recaptcha enterprise admin i  am role  a major benefit of using cloud shell is  that all authentication is handled  automatically  as the cloud shell instance is already  tied to your user account  and its existing credentials however if  this is the first time you run a command  that requires credentials  you will need to authorize cloud shell  first  to perform the key migration you only  need a single command  run gcloud alpha recaptcha keys  migrate and specify the v2 or v3  recaptcha site key you wish to migrate  and the project id of the cloud project  where you enabled the recaptcha  enterprise api  earlier you should see a confirmation  that your key has been successfully  migrated  back in the cloud console we can see our  migrated key under security  recaptcha enterprise here we can see  analytics and manage the key moving  forward  and that is how you can easily migrate  your existing recaptcha v2 and v3 site  keys  to recaptcha enterprise for truly  frictionless security  to learn more about recaptcha enterprise  go to cloud.google.com  recaptcha dash enterprise  you

